MMV(1)                         ZOAU Command Syntax                        MMV(1)

NAME

	mmv - Move (rename) a partitioned dataset member to a new name.

SYNOPSIS

	mmv [-dhv] DATASET OLD_MEM NEW_MEM

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	Move (rename) a member in DATASET from name OLD_MEM to NEW_MEM. The member
	is not copied; it is strictly renamed. This command will not rename datasets.
	Use the dmv command to rename a dataset.

	mmv supports moving members from partitioned generation datasets by relative
	or absolute name notation.

EXAMPLES

EXIT VALUES

  	0
  		mmv ran successfully.

  	other
		Error occurred. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO
	mv(1), dmv(1), dcp(1)
